First on the line, always. Full state name straight from
`biomechanical-input-interface-modeline-state-name' — the bar never keeps
its own copy, so the two can never disagree. Empty before the
keyboard assigns a state.
#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(manifolding-modeline-define-segment keyboard-state
  (propertize
   (or (and (fboundp 'biomechanical-input-interface-modeline-state-name)
            (biomechanical-input-interface-modeline-state-name))
       "")
   'face 'manifolding-modeline-keyboard-face))
#+end_src
